> is x odd and x even?
  note: "odd": read as an odd function, f(-x) = -f(x), not an odd number for every input (say "an odd function" or "always odd")
  ucas: it(x) = x where x % 2 == 0
  ucas: parity it
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
parity of it:
  odd: f(-x) = -f(x)
  not even: f(x) = 2, f(-x) = -2 at x = 2
  proved, exhaustive over every x with -x in the domain
